# DianaSh golden corpus. Recorded from the C# shell, byte for byte, and frozen since its recorder went with the C# core host on 2026-11-07 - see EmuSen_DianaSh.md §13.4.
# Patterns: <ROOT> is the sandbox's real root, <TEMP> the corpus's real temporary folder, <INSTALL> the install's real directory;
# a 'match' block is a regular expression the whole output must match, written where a line prints a time or a measured number.
command runto
usage 1   runto nmi | irq | brk | cop   resume until the next interrupt of that kind is taken
usage 2   runto scanline <n>            resume until scanline <n> starts
usage 3   runto frame [<n>]             resume until frame <n> (default: the next one)
usage 4   runto <addr>                  resume until <addr> executes (a one-shot breakpoint)

case with no target
target none
covers 1
$ runto nmi
out 58
No ROM loaded - this command needs an active debug target.
status 1
action none
$ echo $?
out 1
1
status 0
action none
end
